#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:721
msgid "Before you publish"
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:723
msgid "Give every post a 1200×630 image. In a feed the image is the advertisement and the text is the footnote — a bare link takes a fraction of the space and gets a fraction of the clicks."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:724
msgid "Keep the headline under about 70 characters so a phone shows all of it instead of cutting it mid-sentence."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:725
msgid "Write the excerpt yourself. It becomes the description under the link, and the opening sentence of an article is rarely its best pitch."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:726
msgid "Do not paste the title twice. The share text should be the one sentence that makes somebody stop scrolling — the surprising number, the mistake you made, the thing they can use today."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:727
msgid "End with a question. Comments push a post to people who do not follow you, and the first hour of comments sets the reach for the rest of the day."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:731
msgid "Timing and frequency"
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:733
msgid "Publish when readers are awake. Weekday mornings around 08:00–10:00 and evenings around 19:00–22:00 work for most Hebrew-speaking audiences. The sharing window on the Promotion tab holds a 03:00 post until the morning."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:734
msgid "An Israeli week is not an American week. Friday afternoon and Saturday behave differently here, so check your own numbers before you copy a schedule from a blog post."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:735
msgid "Three good posts a week beat ten thin ones. Networks judge each post by its engagement, so a weak post quietly costs you reach on the next one."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:736
msgid "Reshare evergreen posts after two or three months with a new opening line. Almost nobody saw them the first time."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:740
msgid "Getting it in front of people"
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:742
msgid "Answer every comment in the first hour. It is the cheapest reach you will ever buy."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:743
msgid "Boost only what already works. Putting a small budget behind a post that is doing well organically beats guessing in advance which post deserves it."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:744
msgid "In groups and communities, contribute to the discussion and let the link follow. Dropping links is how accounts get muted."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:745
msgid "For Hebrew-speaking audiences, WhatsApp and Telegram often send more traffic than Facebook, because sharing there is one tap into a private conversation. Keep both buttons switched on."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:746
msgid "Cut one post into several formats: a quote card, a short video, a carousel. Same idea, different surfaces, more chances to be seen."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:750
msgid "Measuring"
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:752
msgid "Tag every link with UTM parameters and judge a network by the sessions it sends, not by the likes it collects."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:753
msgid "Watch clicks and saves rather than reach. Reach is what the network decided to give you; a click is what your audience decided to give you."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:754
msgid "Once a month, look at your three best posts and ask what they had in common. Then do that again on purpose."
msgstr ""

#: social-hub/includes/admin/class-settings-page.php:760
msgid "The short version of what tends to work. The Promotion tab turns most of it into settings, and the box in the post editor checks each post against it before it goes out."
msgstr ""

